# star_wars_2025_le 0.96 - Spike 3 (64-bit ARM): drafted by s3port.py (PAD-1287) from the Spike 3 port star_wars_elg-1.10.port (star_wars_elg 1.10).
# Functions paired across the two titles: 9339 of 18297 reference functions (7763 anchored by vtable slots and strings, 360 through calls that line up, the rest grown through calls); half of them line up 100% or better.
# Written: what the reference port carries that is the FRAMEWORK's (each site's function at least 75% alike its
# reference's, each global and offset read at the lined-up instruction, the engines' layouts re-read off this program's
# own code); the switch lines from this program's own device table. The reference game's own content (shows, lamps,
# callouts, scenes, held coils, its modes) is not this title's: written as comments, for its own port.
# Its switch ids are MEASURED, not the table's ranks (s3port.py --switch-ids, PAD-1290): this program numbers its RIGHT
# TARGET last (87) and every switch after it in the table one lower, so the drafted lines put a press on the wrong shot.
# proofs/s3census.sh pressed each one in a game on the rig (tools/spike3_emu/proofs/titles/star_wars_2025_le-0.96.switch_ids);
# 27 of the 32 reached the modes, the slingshots, pop bumpers and drop target never did and are left out.
# Emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1290) on the Spike 3 rig (s3proof.sh, slot 190, hidden, muted, prebuilt/mode64.so):
# the runtime took this port (29 sites, 27 shots), held back the Insider achievement query (type 28), armed the 6
# events with the dispatch hooked and both switch_hit sites; CLOCK TEST (a mode file: Right target x3, 25 s, Left
# orbit / At-at target / Right orbit) started on the third Right target hit, scored 6 shots through the game's
# score_add (+21,000,000; 12,751,100 -> 36,972,230) and ended when its time ran out, the game playing on to the cap.
# Ball save emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1290, slots 190/191, s3proof.sh PROOF=ballsave): SAVE TEST's 15 s save was taken
# through multiball_serve, the drain inside it served back (trough eject, auto plunger), 3 shots scored 6,000,000 on that
# ball and the drain after the save ended it; the control with no ball_save ended the ball on its first drain, 5.8 s in.
# Multiball emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1290, slot 192, PROOF=mb): 3 balls served through the game's serve, the mode
# ran its 40 s and scored 3 shots, then "ours is over" at one ball. Not seen yet: a `stack no` mode waiting in the
# game's OWN multiball - the rig never started one (Sarlacc pit, Death Star locks and target, Top vuk tried).
# Program sha1 91fb0281b13b607d400fb1b971e9e04c2f71568d (games/game).

game           star_wars_2025_le
version        0.96

